WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.101
Welcome to PrepForCase.

2
00:00:02.121 --> 00:00:06.711
In two minutes: what a case interview is, how the course works, and how to start.

3
00:00:07.061 --> 00:00:10.281
In a case interview, you get a real business problem.

4
00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:13.455
Why are profits falling? Should we enter this market?

5
00:00:13.475 --> 00:00:17.679
You have about half an hour to solve it, out loud, with your interviewer.

6
00:00:18.029 --> 00:00:19.714
There's no single right answer.

7
00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:25.496
They're watching how you think: a clear structure, sound numbers, and a confident recommendation.

8
00:00:25.846 --> 00:00:27.988
Most cases follow six steps.

9
00:00:28.008 --> 00:00:28.826
The prompt.

10
00:00:28.846 --> 00:00:30.332
Your recap and questions.

11
00:00:30.352 --> 00:00:31.285
A structure.

12
00:00:31.305 --> 00:00:32.441
A hypothesis.

13
00:00:32.461 --> 00:00:33.495
The analysis.

14
00:00:33.515 --> 00:00:34.964
And your recommendation.

15
00:00:35.314 --> 00:00:38.711
The course teaches each step, in eleven short lessons.

16
00:00:38.761 --> 00:00:43.041
Module one, Foundations: how interviews work, and the opening.

17
00:00:43.061 --> 00:00:48.939
Module two, Solving the case: structure, maths, charts, sizing, and the recommendation.

18
00:00:48.959 --> 00:00:53.336
Module three, Coming across well: how you sound, and your fit stories.

19
00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:57.814
Each lesson has a worked example, an exercise, and a quick quiz.

20
00:00:58.164 --> 00:01:02.932
Then practise: 102 cases, with a strong answer at every step.

21
00:01:03.032 --> 00:01:05.456
Drill the core skills in ten minutes a day.

22
00:01:05.556 --> 00:01:08.849
And track your prep, so you always know what to fix next.

23
00:01:09.199 --> 00:01:13.875
Add your interview date, and your Home page follows a plan for the time you have.

24
00:01:14.225 --> 00:01:17.067
Start with lesson 1. It takes 8 minutes.

25
00:01:17.087 --> 00:01:18.334
Good luck.
